What:		/proc/oplus_frame_boost/ctrl
What:		/proc/oplus_frame_boost/sys_ctrl
What:		/proc/oplus_frame_boost/stune_boost
What:		/proc/oplus_frame_boost/info
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		OnePlus Frame Boost 3.0 (OFB) control, system-control,
		tuning, and frame-group reporting interfaces.  The ioctl ABI uses
		the donor 9R OFB command layouts and manages UI, render,
		SurfaceFlinger, RenderEngine, and game frame groups.

What:		/proc/sys/kernel/frame_boost_enabled
What:		/proc/sys/kernel/frame_boost_debug
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Exact OnePlus 9R Android 14 Frame Boost sysctl ABI.  Frame Boost is
		enabled by default, matching the donor.  The debug switch defaults
		to zero.

What:		/proc/sys/fbg/frame_boost_safe_mode
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		H.40 emergency rollback extension.  It defaults to zero, so it does
		not alter donor behavior.  Writing one suppresses Frame Boost policy
		while leaving its control nodes available for recovery.

What:		/proc/oplus_cpu/ua_ctrl
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		OnePlus UA control ioctl.  It accepts the Android 14 9R UA status
		command and reports the previous and current Frame Boost utilization
		scales through the donor ua_info_data layout.

What:		/proc/oplus_touch_boost/touch_info
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only current touchpanel BTN_TOUCH state supplied by the 9R UA
		control package.  The value is one while pressed and zero after
		release.
